# Earflow — gesture architecture (mandatory)

Read **`docs/GESTURE_ARCHITECTURE.md`** before any pointer drag/swipe/scroll-handoff change.

## Build correctly from the start (INV-GESTURE-011)

1. **Arbiter:** one owner per `pointerId` (`GestureArbiterProvider` Map) — never a global singleton slot for all fingers.
2. **Session per UI domain:** mini-bar → `useMiniPlayerGestureSession` only; do not wire `usePlayerSheetState` + gestures separately in parents.
3. **Delegate graph:** claim policy in `gestureDelegates.js` — do not duplicate priority/exclusive logic in components.
4. **BottomSheet:** `useSheetDragArbitration` only — no Framer `drag` on sheet (INV-GESTURE-012).
5. **Surfaces:** register in `gestureContracts.js`; use `usePointerGestureMachine` or arbiter-aware hooks; `tryClaim` / `release` on the same `pointerId`.
6. **`touch-action`** on the drag element (INV-FE-004).
7. **No parallel recognizers:** Framer `drag`, raw `touchstart` chains, second local state machine without arbiter.
8. **Recover** (`recoverGestures`, `cancelOwner`) — emergency only.

## Mini-bar zone

- `data-mini-gesture-zone` on shell
- `shouldDeferToMiniPlayerGesture` for non-mini surfaces
- `exclusive` mini claim on `pointer-down`

## Agent disclosure (INV-FE-008 when touching UI)

Same reply: norm (arbiter + coordinator), debt (PEND-GESTURE-*), verify (e2e touch + `data-mini-bar-ui` after deploy).

## Tests

- Unit: `GestureArbiterProvider.test.js`, gesture machine tests
- E2E: real touch helpers; live gate on `data-mini-bar-ui`

Do not reintroduce **global single active owner** or split mini sheet/gesture wiring in `MobilePlayerBar/index.js`.
